    "result_text": "The build passes green. \n\n## Summary\n\nAdded the `initials` field to the Owner response, returning upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the existing `displayName` pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` string `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field plus its getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` computing the value:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\",\n       expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\n`firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty` on the `Person` superclass, so `charAt(0)` is safe. The acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` (john/smith \u2192 `J.S.`) and the full suite pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
